==Latin==

===Etymology===
{{unk|la}}. Possibilities include:
* Cognate with {{cog|sla-pro|*zębnǫti}} and {{cog|lt|žémbėti}}, both meaning “to germinate, sprout”, perhaps from {{der|la|ine-pro|*ǵemb-}} or {{m|ine-pro|*ǵeb-||to bud, sprout}}, though such a root would be irregular for PIE;<ref>{{R:itc:EDL|gemma|257|passage=PIE *ǵeb-m-}}</ref><ref>{{R:sla:EDSIL|543|*zębnǫti II}}</ref>
* From {{m+|ine-pro|*ǵómbʰos|*ǵembʰ-|nail, tooth}}, despite the semantic gap. Compare, however, {{m+|grc|ὄνυξ|t=claw, nail, hoof, talon, but also [[onyx]] (gem)}};
* From {{der|la|itc-pro|*gen-||to produce}}, from {{m+|ine-pro|*ǵenh₁-}}; compare {{m|la|gignō}} and {{m|la|genus}};
* A non-Indo-European {{der|la|qfa-sub}} source. The unusual form of the word, the lack of clear cognates and the semantic category of the word make this hypothesis likely.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA}}

